.TH "sysforge" "1" "2026\-10\-24"
.PP
.PP
.SH NAME
.PP
sysforge \- AUR helper that builds and tracks packages tuned to your CPU
.PP
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\fBsysforge\fR [\fB\-v\fR.\&.\&.\&] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIARGS\fR.\&.\&.\&]
.PP
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
SysForge builds AUR and custom packages with rule\-matched compiler\-flag
profiles: every package is built with the optimization flags its matching
profile resolves (\-march=native, LTO, linker choice, caches), while pacman
remains the owner of the package database.\& Build metadata (versions, the
resolved flags, toolchain identity, source provenance, and the reviewed
source commit) is recorded per package in build_state.\&toml and drives
update, drift detection, and diagnostics.\&
.PP
\fBsysforge update\fR is the steady\-state entry point: it walks the live install
set (all foreign packages, plus repo packages selected by overrides or
repo_mode = "build_from_source"), syncs sources, reports drift, and rebuilds
what changed.\& A changed source is shown as a diff for approval before it is
built (the PKGBUILD review gate), and at a terminal the whole plan is shown
before anything changes.\&
.PP
\fBsysforge run\fR builds by stage: \fBrun toolchain\fR an optionally PGO\- and
BOLT\-optimized LLVM toolchain, \fBrun kernel\fR a custom kernel under boot\-safety
gates, and \fBrun packages\fR everything in packages.\&toml.\& \fBrun pipeline\fR is the
fresh\-install bootstrap, from an Arch ISO environment through every stage.\&
.PP
\fBsysforge doctor\fR is the read\-only health check: \fBdoctor system\fR for the
running system (bare \fBsysforge doctor\fR is the same sweep), \fBdoctor pkg\fR for
individual packages.\&
.PP
Install\-bearing commands write a stage sentinel before mutating the system;
an interrupted run is detected on the next invocation and offers a recorded
recovery command.\&
.PP
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.PP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
.RS 4
Increase verbosity.\& Default shows errors only; \-v adds warnings, \-vv
informational messages, \-vvv debug output (repeatable, position
independent).\& The default level (when no flag is passed) can be raised
via the \fB[log] verbosity\fR key in \fIsysforge.\&toml\fR; a CLI flag always wins.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-quiet\fR
.RS 4
Suppress all non\-error output (verbosity 0), overriding both \fB\-v\fR and
the \fB[log] verbosity\fR config default.\& File logs still record every
level.\& Distinct from \fBdoctor\fR'\&s local \fB\-\-quiet\fR (which suppresses clean
diagnostic lines).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
.RS 4
Print the sysforge version and exit.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-py\-profile\fR
.RS 4
Run the verb under the Python profiler (cProfile) and print the top
functions by cumulative time to stderr at exit.\& Position independent.\&
Profiles sysforge'\&s own runtime only; subprocess work (makepkg, pacman,
git) appears as wait time; use \fB\-\-timings\fR for wall\-clock phase costs.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-py\-profile\-out\fR \fIFILE\fR
.RS 4
Write raw cProfile stats to \fIFILE\fR for later analysis (pstats,
snakeviz).\& Implies \fB\-\-py\-profile\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-timings\fR
.RS 4
Print a wall\-clock phase timing report (source sync, version check,
drift detection, per\-package builds, install, pacman \-Syu) after
\fBbuild\fR and \fBupdate\fR runs.\& Without the flag the report is still
written to the log at info level.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-color\fR \fIauto\fR|\fIalways\fR|\fInever\fR
.RS 4
Colorize output.\& \fIauto\fR (the default) colours when writing to a
terminal and honours the \fBNO_COLOR\fR and \fBFORCE_COLOR\fR environment
variables; \fIalways\fR forces colour on (useful when piping into a pager
such as \fBless \-R\fR); \fInever\fR disables it.\& Overrides the \fB[ui] color\fR
key in \fIsysforge.\&toml\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-no\-throttle\fR
.RS 4
Ignore the configured build throttle (\fBnice\fR/\fBionice\fR/\fBcpu_quota\fR/\fBjobs\fR
from \fB[build]\fR) for this run, building at normal unthrottled priority.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-turbo\fR
.RS 4
Run the build at \fIhigher\fR than default priority: negative niceness and
best\-effort IO, with no CPU ceiling or job cap.\& Stronger than
\fB\-\-no\-throttle\fR.\& Lowering niceness may require privilege; when the kernel
refuses, the build runs at the current priority (best\-effort, never fatal).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-frozen\fR
.RS 4
Source freeze: refuse all new source downloads (AUR clones, git fetches,
VCS version probes) for this run.\& Existing checkouts still build.\&
Overrides \fB[security] freeze_sources = false\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-no\-frozen\fR
.RS 4
Lift the source freeze for this run, overriding
\fB[security] freeze_sources = true\fR.\& Wins over \fB\-\-frozen\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-thaw\fR \fIPKG\fR[,\fIPKG\fR.\&.\&.\&]
.RS 4
Exempt the named pkgbases from the source freeze; everything else stays
frozen.\& Repeatable, and accepts a comma\-separated list.\& Run\-scoped only:
there is no persistent trust list.\&
.PP
.RE
.SH SHARED OPTIONS
.PP
Options that mean the same in every command that takes them.\& Each command
under COMMANDS names the ones it accepts in its \fBShared options\fR line.\&
.PP
\fB\-\-abi\-check\fR
.RS 4
Run a post\-build ABI compatibility check on built shared libraries.\&
Used by: \fBrun pipeline\fR, \fBrun toolchain\fR, \fBrun packages\fR, \fBrun kernel\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-cache\-report\fR
.RS 4
Print a structured cache summary after the run.\&
Used by: \fBrun pipeline\fR, \fBrun toolchain\fR, \fBrun packages\fR, \fBrun kernel\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-cleansrc\-force\fR
.RS 4
Like \-\-cleansrc but bypasses the dirty/diverged guard and overwrites the local clone unconditionally.\& Use when the upstream rewrote history (e.\&g.\& Arch packaging repos force\-push every release) and the local commits have no value to preserve.\&
Used by: \fBbuild\fR, \fBupdate\fR, \fBfetch\fR, \fBrun toolchain\fR, \fBrun kernel\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-config\-dir\fR \fIDIR\fR
.RS 4
Live config dir (default: $SYSFORGE_CONFIG_DIR, else /etc/sysforge).\&
Used by: \fBconfig check\fR, \fBconfig clean\fR, \fBconfig reset\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
.RS 4
Show what would run without executing anything.\&
Used by: \fBrun pipeline\fR, \fBrun toolchain\fR, \fBrun packages\fR, \fBrun kernel\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-json\fR
.RS 4
Print one JSON document (schema 1) on stdout instead of the report: each axis'\&s findings and the checks it ran and skipped.\& Everything else goes to stderr; the exit code is unchanged.\&
Used by: \fBdoctor system\fR, \fBdoctor pkg\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-log\-dir\fR \fIDIR\fR
.RS 4
Directory for log files.\&
Used by: \fBrun pipeline\fR, \fBrun packages\fR, \fBrun kernel\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-no\-llvm\-preflight\fR
.RS 4
Suppress the LLVM source pre\-flight summary.\&
Used by: \fBbuild\fR, \fBupdate\fR, \fBfetch\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-no\-pager\fR
.RS 4
Don'\&t pipe output through $PAGER (default: paginate when stdout is a TTY).\&
Used by: \fBlog\fR, \fBstate list\fR, \fBstate orphans\fR, \fBstate profiles\fR, \fBstate boot\-entries\fR, \fBstate failed\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-no\-pkg\-log\fR
.RS 4
Disable per\-package log files.\&
Used by: \fBbuild\fR, \fBupdate\fR, \fBrun pipeline\fR, \fBrun packages\fR, \fBrun kernel\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-packages\fR \fIFILE\fR
.RS 4
Path to packages.\&toml (default: /etc/sysforge/packages.\&toml; override the dir with $SYSFORGE_CONFIG_DIR).\&
Used by: \fBupdate\fR, \fBpackages list\fR, \fBpackages add\fR, \fBpackages add\-group\fR, \fBpackages remove\fR, \fBrun pipeline\fR, \fBrun packages\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-persist\-log\fR
.RS 4
Keep log files after successful completion.\&
Used by: \fBupdate\fR, \fBrun pipeline\fR, \fBrun toolchain\fR, \fBrun packages\fR, \fBrun kernel\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-profile\-conf\fR \fIFILE\fR
.RS 4
Path to a profiles.\&toml to use instead of the default.\&
Used by: \fBbuild\fR, \fBupdate\fR, \fBfetch\fR, \fBresolve\fR, \fBrun pipeline\fR, \fBrun packages\fR, \fBrun kernel\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-retry\-failed\fR
.RS 4
Retry all failed packages without prompting.\&
Used by: \fBrun pipeline\fR, \fBrun packages\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-state\-dir\fR \fIDIR\fR
.RS 4
Override state directory.\&
Used by: \fBbuild\fR, \fBupdate\fR, \fBstate list\fR, \fBstate repair\fR, \fBstate failed\fR, \fBstate forget\fR, \fBrun pipeline\fR, \fBrun hardware\fR, \fBrun reconfigure\fR, \fBrun toolchain\fR, \fBrun packages\fR, \fBrun kernel\fR, \fBrevert\-to\-stock\fR, \fBuninstall\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-yes\fR
.RS 4
Write without asking (needed without a terminal).\&
Used by: \fBconfig clean\fR, \fBconfig reset\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
.SH COMMANDS
.PP
.SS build
.PP
\fBsysforge build\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIPKGBUILD.\&.\&.\&\fR
.PP
Build a package from a PKGBUILD.\&
.PP
\fBPKGBUILD\fR
.RS 4
One or more packages to build (path, directory, or bare package name).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-makepkg\fR, \fB\-m\fR \fIFLAGS\fR
.RS 4
Additional makepkg flags, appended after profile makepkg_flags.\& Usually optional: bare makepkg short flags are forwarded implicitly (sysforge build PKGBUILD \-sfc works without \-m).\& \-m is only needed for makepkg long flags (e.\&g.\& \-\-skippgpcheck), flags that take a value (\-p, \-D), or flags sysforge claims for itself (\-h, \-V).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-interactive\fR
.RS 4
Strip \-\-noconfirm from profile makepkg_flags and hand stdout/stderr to makepkg'\&s terminal so pacman conflict prompts and other unbuffered interactive output appear immediately (disables line\-based output classification while set).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-persist\-log\fR
.RS 4
Keep the per\-package log file after a successful build.\& Also settable via [build] persist_log = true in packages.\&toml.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-log\-dir\fR \fIDIR\fR
.RS 4
Directory for the per\-package log file (default: alongside the PKGBUILD).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-toolchain\fR \fIgcc\fR|\fIllvm\fR
.RS 4
Build the named packages with this compiler toolchain as a whole (compilers, binutils and linker) instead of their profile'\&s, for this build.\& Dependencies keep their own.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-save\-toolchain\fR
.RS 4
With \-\-toolchain: also save it for these packages in profiles.\&toml [package_compiler_overrides], so later builds and updates use it too.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-reset\-toolchain\fR
.RS 4
Remove these packages'\& saved toolchain from profiles.\&toml, so they build with their profile'\&s again.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-cc\fR \fICOMPILER\fR
.RS 4
Override only CC (C compiler) for this build, e.\&g.\& \-\-cc clang\-19.\& A gcc/g++ or clang/clang++ pair with \-\-cxx acts as \-\-toolchain.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-cxx\fR \fICOMPILER\fR
.RS 4
Override only CXX (C++ compiler) for this build, e.\&g.\& \-\-cxx clang++\-19.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-ld\fR \fILINKER\fR
.RS 4
Override linker for this build, e.\&g.\& \-\-ld lld.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-cache\-report\fR
.RS 4
Print a structured cache summary (ccache/sccache hit rates) after the build.\& Also settable via [build] cache_report = true in packages.\&toml.\& Builds run in the build sandbox show n/a: they never use the host caches.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-abi\-check\fR
.RS 4
Run a post\-build ABI compatibility check on built shared libraries.\& Also settable via [build] abi_check = true in packages.\&toml.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-no\-update\fR
.RS 4
Skip the source sync (fetch and fast\-forward) and build the PKGBUILD as checked out.\& \-\-cleansrc still syncs.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-cleansrc\fR
.RS 4
Purge the package src dir and re\-clone before building.\& Refuses (per package) if the existing clone has uncommitted changes, ahead\-of\-upstream commits, or no upstream tracking branch.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-review\fR
.RS 4
Review changed sources of every type, including those trusted by [build] review_trusted_sources (by default Arch'\&s own packaging repos).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-no\-review\fR
.RS 4
Skip the PKGBUILD review gate (full source\-tree diff prompt for packages whose source changed since the last accepted review).\& Also configurable via [build] review = false in packages.\&toml.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-force\fR
.RS 4
Unconditionally build all arguments from source for this run only, including repo packages not yet opted in.\& Never prompts for or modifies packages.\&toml opt\-in keys.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-rebuild\fR
.RS 4
Force makepkg to rebuild even when a matching package already exists in PKGDEST (passes \-f).\& Use after a toolchain or build\-flag change, where the version is unchanged so makepkg would otherwise skip the build and reinstall the stale artifact.\& Note \-\-force is unrelated: it only waives the repo\-package opt\-in gate.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-pgo\fR \fIrecord\fR|\fIuse\fR
.RS 4
Instrumentation PGO (LLVM toolchain only).\& \-\-pgo=record builds+installs an instrumented package that writes profile data to the sysforge store as you run its workloads; \-\-pgo=use merges the collected profiles and rebuilds an optimized <pkg>\-sysforge (conflicts/replaces the stock package).\& Aimed at mesa; any other target warns unless listed in sysforge.\&toml [pgo] allow.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBShared options:\fR \fB\-\-no\-pkg\-log\fR, \fB\-\-profile\-conf\fR, \fB\-\-cleansrc\-force\fR, \fB\-\-no\-llvm\-preflight\fR, \fB\-\-state\-dir\fR (see SHARED OPTIONS)
.PP
\fBConfiguration:\fR profiles.\&toml, packages.\&toml ([build]), sysforge.\&toml ([git])
.PP
\fBEnvironment:\fR $SYSFORGE_CONFIG_DIR, $SYSFORGE_STATE_DIR, $PAGER (review diffs)
.PP
.SS update
.PP
\fBsysforge update\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fI[PKG.\&.\&.\&]\fR
.PP
Check for and rebuild outdated sysforge\-managed packages.\&
.PP
\fBPKG\fR
.RS 4
Limit update to these package names (default: all sysforge\-managed packages).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
.RS 4
Show what would be rebuilt without doing it.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-json\fR
.RS 4
With \-\-dry\-run: print one JSON document (schema 1) on stdout instead of the summary: each package'\&s verdict and both drift axes.\& Everything else goes to stderr; the exit code is unchanged.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-devel\fR
.RS 4
Resolve and rebuild VCS packages (\-git, \-svn, \-hg, \-bzr) whose upstream HEAD has advanced past the installed version.\& Resolution runs makepkg \-\-nobuild per VCS package; up\-to\-date packages are skipped, not rebuilt.\& Per\-package upstream commits recorded in build_state are reused on subsequent runs to short\-circuit the resolve via git ls\-remote.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-offline\fR
.RS 4
No network: skip the source sync, clones, and AUR RPC.\& Pure local version check.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-install\-only\fR
.RS 4
Skip rebuild; install only those locally\-built artifacts in PKGDEST that are newer than the installed version.\& Implies \-\-offline.\& Mutually exclusive with \-\-makepkg, \-\-no\-cleanbuild, \-\-cleansrc, \-\-cleansrc\-force, \-\-interactive, and \-\-cache\-report.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-cache\-report\fR
.RS 4
Print a structured cache summary after the run.\& Builds run in the build sandbox show n/a: they never use the host caches.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-log\-dir\fR \fIDIR\fR
.RS 4
Directory for per\-package log files.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-makepkg\fR, \fB\-m\fR \fIFLAGS\fR
.RS 4
Extra flags passed verbatim to makepkg.\& Usually optional: bare makepkg short flags are forwarded implicitly (sysforge update \-f works without \-m).\& \-m is only needed for makepkg long flags (e.\&g.\& \-\-skippgpcheck), flags that take a value (\-p, \-D), or flags sysforge claims for itself (\-h, \-V).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-yes\fR
.RS 4
Do not ask before changing anything: confirm the plan (update asks at a terminal by default; [build] confirm_plan in packages.\&toml).\& Does not accept PKGBUILD review prompts.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-interactive\fR
.RS 4
Pause on build failures to allow manual correction (default: log failure and continue), and let the trailing pacman \-Syu ask its confirmation prompts (default: \-\-noconfirm).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-no\-cleanbuild\fR
.RS 4
Skip the automatic \-\-cleanbuild (\-C) added for update runs.\& Useful when packages are already built and you only need to re\-run the install step.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-cleansrc\fR
.RS 4
Purge each package'\&s src dir and re\-clone before building.\& Per\-package fatal if the clone has uncommitted changes, ahead\-of\-upstream commits, or no upstream.\& That package is reported failed and the run continues.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-review\fR
.RS 4
Review changed sources of every type, including trusted ones (by default Arch'\&s own packaging repos).\& Without this flag, update prompts at a terminal for untrusted changes and refuses them with no terminal.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-no\-review\fR
.RS 4
Skip the PKGBUILD review gate entirely.\& Also configurable via [build] review = false in packages.\&toml.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-sysupgrade\fR
.RS 4
Finish the run with a single `pacman \-Syu` system upgrade, after source\-built artifacts are installed (they stay protected by the `IgnoreGroup = sf\-build` line `sysforge setup` adds).\& Independent of repo_mode: no extra packages enter the version\-check walk.\& Also settable via [build] system_upgrade = true in packages.\&toml.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-no\-sysupgrade\fR
.RS 4
Skip the trailing system upgrade even when [build] system_upgrade = true is set in packages.\&toml.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-no\-sysupgrade\-report\fR
.RS 4
Skip the version\-change report for the trailing system upgrade.\& The report is on by default and applies only to the \-\-sysupgrade / [build] system_upgrade route (the classified pacman\-class list already itemizes itself); it snapshots the local package DB either side of the transaction and prints one `pkg: old \-> new` line per change, capped at the default verbosity and printed in full under \-v.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-no\-toolchain\-preflight\fR
.RS 4
Skip the toolchain pre\-flight (rust/cmake/meson availability + lib32 cross targets) that normally runs before the build loop.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-include\-stage\-owned\fR
.RS 4
Include packages owned by `run kernel` or `run toolchain` (e.\&g.\& the kernel'\&s `linux\-sysforge`).\& Skipped by default; the owning command (`sysforge run kernel`) is the canonical update path.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-versions\fR
.RS 4
List packages with a newer version available and exit.\& Read\-only: no source sync beyond the version check, no rebuild, no stage.\& Unlike a normal run this always includes stage\-owned (toolchain/kernel) packages, annotated with the stage that owns them.\& It is the quick answer to '\&is there a new toolchain or kernel?\&'\& without entering `run toolchain` / `run kernel`.\& Up\-to\-date packages collapse into a count.\& VCS packages report no available version unless \-\-devel is also passed.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-explain\-drift\fR
.RS 4
List drifted packages and exit, across both axes: toolchain drift (recorded toolchain_variant differs from the active gcc / stock_llvm / pgo_llvm) and flag drift (profiled packages whose flags now resolve differently than when built, with a per\-key diff).\& Informational; no source sync, no rebuild.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-rebuild\-on\-toolchain\-drift\fR
.RS 4
Treat toolchain\-variant drift as an upgrade trigger: packages built under a different toolchain than is active now are added to the rebuild queue.\& Off by default: drift is reported but not acted on, since most C/C++ packages don'\&t measurably benefit from a re\-stamp.\& Also settable via [update] rebuild_on_toolchain_drift = true in sysforge.\&toml.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-rebuild\-on\-flag\-drift\fR
.RS 4
Treat flag drift as an upgrade trigger: profiled packages whose flags now resolve differently than when built are added to the rebuild queue.\& Off by default: flag drift is reported but not acted on, since one profile edit can drift every profiled package.\& Also settable via [update] rebuild_on_flag_drift = true in sysforge.\&toml.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-rebuild\-on\-drift\fR
.RS 4
Umbrella for both \-\-rebuild\-on\-toolchain\-drift and \-\-rebuild\-on\-flag\-drift: rebuild anything that has drifted.\& Also settable via [update] rebuild_on_drift = true in sysforge.\&toml.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBShared options:\fR \fB\-\-packages\fR, \fB\-\-state\-dir\fR, \fB\-\-profile\-conf\fR, \fB\-\-no\-pkg\-log\fR, \fB\-\-persist\-log\fR, \fB\-\-cleansrc\-force\fR, \fB\-\-no\-llvm\-preflight\fR (see SHARED OPTIONS)
.PP
\fBConfiguration:\fR profiles.\&toml, packages.\&toml, sysforge.\&toml ([git], failure_handling)
.PP
\fBEnvironment:\fR $SYSFORGE_CONFIG_DIR, $SYSFORGE_STATE_DIR, $PAGER (review diffs)
.PP
.SS fetch
.PP
\fBsysforge fetch\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIPKG.\&.\&.\&\fR
.PP
Download PKGBUILD(s) into pkgbuild_src_dir without building.\&
.PP
\fBPKG\fR
.RS 4
One or more package names to download.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-no\-update\fR
.RS 4
Skip the source sync (fetch and fast\-forward) for packages that are already cloned.\& \-\-cleansrc still syncs.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-cleansrc\fR
.RS 4
Purge each package'\&s src dir and re\-clone.\& Refuses (per package) if the existing clone has uncommitted changes, ahead\-of\-upstream commits, or no upstream tracking branch.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBShared options:\fR \fB\-\-cleansrc\-force\fR, \fB\-\-no\-llvm\-preflight\fR, \fB\-\-profile\-conf\fR (see SHARED OPTIONS)
.PP
\fBConfiguration:\fR profiles.\&toml ([paths]), sysforge.\&toml ([git])
.PP
\fBEnvironment:\fR $SYSFORGE_CONFIG_DIR
.PP
.SS search
.PP
\fBsysforge search\fR \fITERM\fR
.PP
Search installed, repo, and AUR packages for a term.\&
.PP
\fBTERM\fR
.RS 4
Search term (matches name and description).\&
.PP
.RE
.SS help
.PP
\fBsysforge help\fR \fI[COMMAND.\&.\&.\&]\fR
.PP
Print help for sysforge or for a COMMAND (alias for \-\-help).\&
.PP
\fBCOMMAND\fR
.RS 4
Command (and optional subcommand) to describe, e.\&g.\& `sysforge help state failed`.\& Omit for top\-level help.\&
.PP
.RE
.SS doctor
.PP
\fBsysforge doctor\fR \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
.PP
Diagnose system health (`doctor system`) or package health (`doctor pkg`).\& Bare `doctor` runs the full system sweep.\&
.PP
\fBConfiguration:\fR profiles.\&toml; toolchain.\&toml and kernel.\&toml on their axes
.PP
\fBEnvironment:\fR $SYSFORGE_CONFIG_DIR, $SYSFORGE_STATE_DIR
.PP
.SS doctor system
.PP
\fBsysforge doctor system\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.PP
System\-state axes: toolchain, cache, hardware, graphics, pacman, state, config, boot, restart, storage, services, audio, network, distro.\& With no axis flag, runs all 14 non\-opt\-in axes.\&
.PP
\fB\-\-graphics\fR
.RS 4
Run graphics system\-state probes: nvidia\-drm modeset, driver version skew, Wayland explicit\-sync protocol, Steam GPU accel, and session type.\& Does not select packages: for the graphics package set use `doctor pkg \-\-graphics`.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-gfxperf\fR
.RS 4
Advisory graphics\-performance sweep (stutter/tearing/frame\-drop contributors: video\-decode path, GPU power/clocks, CPU governor, frame pacing, thermal).\& Opt\-in; never fails.\& Combine with \-\-graphics for the full graphics picture.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-hardware\fR
.RS 4
Run system\-state hardware probes: inventory all PCI/USB devices, flag any present device with no kernel driver bound, and audit the running kernel'\&s .\&config for boot\-critical / device\-driver gaps (the missing\-driver class of bug).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-distro\fR
.RS 4
Report the running distribution and its support tier, read from os\-release(5): Arch is the primary base, an Arch\-derived distro (ID_LIKE=arch) has its packaging/dependency/makepkg.\&conf invariants validated but not the bootstrap/kernel/graphics checks, and anything else warns.\& Read\-only, no subprocess; on plain Arch the bare sweep stays silent, this flag always prints the identity.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-toolchain\fR
.RS 4
Check that the configured toolchain matches what'\&s installed: when toolchain.\&toml requests a custom LLVM toolchain (compiler = llvm, optionally PGO) but stock repo LLVM is installed, or the PGO profdata is version\-skewed, report it.\& Also report installed programs that no longer load against the system libLLVM (e.\&g.\& after building it with fewer LLVM targets).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-rust\fR
.RS 4
Report which Rust toolchain a build will actually use: the effective cargo/rustc owner (rustup channel or distro `rust` package) and a WARN if the active rustup default is non\-stable (nightly/beta/pinned).\& Advisory, read\-only; never fails, never rewrites a pin.\& Opt\-in.\& For per\-package rust\-toolchain.\&toml pins use `doctor pkg PKG \-\-rust`.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-cache\fR
.RS 4
Check compile\-cache readiness *before* a build relies on it: whether ccache/sccache are installed, their cache dir is writable, and a non\-zero size cap is set.\& Absence is informational, not a failure.\& Distinct from build verbs'\& \-\-cache\-report, which measures per\-package hit rates *after* a build.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-pacman\fR
.RS 4
Check local package\-database integrity (read\-only, never syncs): `pacman \-Dk` dependency consistency, a stale db.\&lck, unmerged .\&pacnew/.\&pacsave config files under /etc, and orphan packages.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-state\fR
.RS 4
Check sysforge'\&s own state integrity: recorded build failures, an interrupted stage sentinel from a prior run, and build_state drift vs the live pacman database.\& Read\-only (does not recover).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-config\fR
.RS 4
Check the live config files for settings sysforge retired or does not know (the same report as `sysforge config check`).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-boot\fR
.RS 4
Check running\-system boot readiness (reusing the kernel stage'\&s safety primitives): per\-kernel boot artifacts (vmlinuz + initramfs + boot entry), a recovery fallback kernel, /boot space, and DKMS modules for the running kernel.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-restart\fR
.RS 4
Check whether upgraded packages have actually taken effect: scans running processes for files replaced on disk (a `(deleted)` mapping) and reports whether the fix is a unit restart, a re\-login, or a reboot.\& Read\-only; never escalates, so coverage of other users'\& processes is reported as incomplete rather than prompting.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-storage\fR
.RS 4
Check storage/filesystem health: free space on the build dir (warns under [doctor] disk_low_gb) and /etc/fstab integrity (entries whose UUID/label/device no longer resolves).\& Read\-only; never mounts.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-services\fR
.RS 4
Check live service/driver runtime health: failed systemd units (`systemctl \-\-failed`), firmware a driver requested but could not load this boot, and error\-priority journal lines this boot.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-audio\fR
.RS 4
Check live PipeWire/WirePlumber sound\-stack health: failed audio user services (`systemctl \-\-user \-\-failed`) and a vanished output sink (only the dummy auto_null device present).\& User\-scoped, so it degrades to clean under sudo.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-network\fR
.RS 4
Check network/connectivity configuration: no default route, connection\-manager ownership conflicts (more than one of NetworkManager/systemd\-networkd/dhcpcd/… enabled), and a DNS provisioner conflict (systemd\-resolved active but /etc/resolv.\&conf is a static override).\& Read\-only; no live network calls.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-integrity\fR
.RS 4
Verify package\-owned files against alpm'\&s recorded mtree via `pacman \-Qkk`: files an admin or a misbehaving install script altered or removed outside a pacman transaction.\& Opt\-in (excluded from the bare/full sweep because a whole\-system scan re\-hashes every packaged file); scope it with `doctor pkg PKG \-\-integrity`.\& Read\-only; never restores.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-findings\-only\fR
.RS 4
Suppress clean lines; print only findings.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBShared options:\fR \fB\-\-json\fR (see SHARED OPTIONS)
.PP
.SS doctor pkg
.PP
\fBsysforge doctor pkg\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fI[PKG.\&.\&.\&]\fR
.PP
Package\-scoped axes over one or more targets: \-\-abi (depends + ABI linkage), \-\-rust (rust\-toolchain.\&toml pins), \-\-integrity (pacman \-Qkk).\& With no axis flag, runs all three.\&
.PP
\fBPKG\fR
.RS 4
Installed package names to check.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-abi\fR
.RS 4
Walk each target'\&s depends and ABI linkage: unsatisfied dependencies and unresolved sonames, over the transitive dependency closure unless \-\-shallow.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-rust\fR
.RS 4
Report each target'\&s rust\-toolchain.\&toml pin and whether that toolchain is installed (uninstalled = mid\-build network fetch).\& A named target with no PKGBUILD or no pin is reported as such.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-integrity\fR
.RS 4
Verify each target'\&s package\-owned files against alpm'\&s recorded mtree via `pacman \-Qkk`.\& Read\-only; never restores.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-all\fR
.RS 4
Target every installed package, foreign and non\-foreign (pacman \-Q).\& Suppresses the opt\-in axes: runs \-\-abi only unless you name another axis explicitly.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-repo\fR
.RS 4
Target every non\-foreign (native repo) package.\& Narrower than \-\-all; suppresses the opt\-in axes the same way.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-graphics\fR
.RS 4
Target the installed graphics stack (mesa, vulkan, libglvnd, wayland, libdrm, libva, libvdpau, egl\-wayland, xwayland, gamescope, plus per\-vendor drivers from the hardware overlay'\&s gpu_vendors).\& A peer of \-\-all / \-\-repo.\& For graphics system\-state probes use `doctor system \-\-graphics`.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-shallow\fR
.RS 4
Do not recurse into transitive dependencies of each target.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-findings\-only\fR
.RS 4
Suppress clean lines; print only packages with issues.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-suggest\fR, \fB\-s\fR
.RS 4
For each unsatisfied soname, look up candidate packages via `pacman \-Fq`.\& Findings split into '\&install candidates'\& (missing from disk: install the package), '\&rebuild candidates'\& (installed; rebuild against the current system), and '\&ABI\-drift candidates'\& (present but one of their versioned symbols no longer resolves: rebuild or upgrade, not reinstall).\& Requires a synced files db (`sudo pacman \-Fy`).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-apply\fR
.RS 4
Hand the rebuild candidates from \-\-suggest off to `sysforge update` and rebuild them.\& Implies \-\-suggest.\& Rebuilds only: install candidates are printed but not installed.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-yes\fR
.RS 4
Skip the y/N prompt before \-\-apply rebuilds.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
.RS 4
Report what \-\-apply would rebuild without invoking the build.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBShared options:\fR \fB\-\-json\fR (see SHARED OPTIONS)
.PP
.SS resolve
.PP
\fBsysforge resolve\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIPKG\fR
.PP
Show which profile would be applied to a package and why.\&
.PP
\fBPKG\fR
.RS 4
Path to a PKGBUILD file, or bare package name.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-show\-flags\fR
.RS 4
Print the full resolved flag set.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-deps\fR
.RS 4
Show transitive dependency tree with build order instead of profile info.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBShared options:\fR \fB\-\-profile\-conf\fR (see SHARED OPTIONS)
.PP
\fBConfiguration:\fR profiles.\&toml
.PP
\fBEnvironment:\fR $SYSFORGE_CONFIG_DIR
.PP
.SS env
.PP
\fBsysforge env\fR
.PP
Print the inherited env chain, all contributing sources (shell init files, systemd\-user, PAM env, sysforge [defaults] profile), and a mismatches block when sources disagree.\& \-vv adds inline per\-var divergence annotations.\&
.PP
\fBConfiguration:\fR profiles.\&toml
.PP
\fBEnvironment:\fR $SYSFORGE_CONFIG_DIR
.PP
.SS log
.PP
\fBsysforge log\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fI[PKG]\fR
.PP
Page a sysforge log (unified, per\-package or per\-verb) through $PAGER.\&
.PP
\fBPKG\fR
.RS 4
Package name (resolves to <pkgbuild_src_dir>/<pkg>/sysforge_<pkg>.\&log).\& Omit to page the unified log.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-verb\fR \fIVERB\fR
.RS 4
Page the log the last run of VERB left, spelled with dashes (build, update, state\-repair, run\-toolchain, .\&.\&.\&).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-log\-dir\fR \fIDIR\fR
.RS 4
Look in DIR instead, for a log written with the same \-\-log\-dir.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-state\-dir\fR \fIDIR\fR
.RS 4
Override state directory (used to locate the unified and verb logs).\&
.PP
.RE
\fBShared options:\fR \fB\-\-no\-pager\fR (see SHARED OPTIONS)
.PP
\fBConfiguration:\fR profiles.\&toml ([paths] pkgbuild_src_dir, for per\-package logs)
.PP
\fBEnvironment:\fR $SYSFORGE_STATE_DIR, $PAGER
.PP
.SS state
.PP
\fBsysforge state\fR \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
.PP
Inspect or repair build_state.\&toml (live install\-state mirror).\&
.PP
\fBConfiguration:\fR build_state.\&toml under the state directory
.PP
\fBEnvironment:\fR $SYSFORGE_STATE_DIR, $PAGER
.PP
.SS state list
.PP
\fBsysforge state list\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.PP
Tabulate build_state.\&toml entries.\&
.PP
\fB\-\-json\fR
.RS 4
Print one JSON document (schema 1) on stdout instead of the table: recorded packages, opted\-out packages and untracked foreign packages.\& Never paged.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBShared options:\fR \fB\-\-state\-dir\fR, \fB\-\-no\-pager\fR (see SHARED OPTIONS)
.PP
.SS state repair
.PP
\fBsysforge state repair\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.PP
Repair build_state.\&toml: re\-parse PKGBUILDs to rewrite entries with unexpanded shell variables (e.\&g.\& '\&$_pkgname\-git'\&), and normalize known legacy build_mode tokens ('\&profiled'\& \-> '\&source_built'\&).\&
.PP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
.RS 4
Show the planned repair without writing.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBShared options:\fR \fB\-\-state\-dir\fR (see SHARED OPTIONS)
.PP
.SS state orphans
.PP
\fBsysforge state orphans\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.PP
List (and optionally delete) stale .\&pkg.\&tar* artifacts in PKGDEST.\& Only surfaces superseded files (pkgname installed AND artifact older than installed) so \-\-delete is always safe.\&
.PP
\fB\-\-delete\fR
.RS 4
Delete the listed superseded artifacts (prompts for confirmation).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-yes\fR
.RS 4
With \-\-delete: delete without the y/N prompt.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBShared options:\fR \fB\-\-no\-pager\fR (see SHARED OPTIONS)
.PP
.SS state profiles
.PP
\fBsysforge state profiles\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.PP
List the collected optimization profiles (PGO, AutoFDO, Propeller, BOLT) with size, age and collected version.\& Read\-only unless \-\-delete.\&
.PP
\fB\-\-delete\fR \fISTORE\fR
.RS 4
Delete one profile store, METHOD or METHOD/TARGET as listed (e.\&g.\& pgo/mesa, autofdo/linux\-sysforge); asks for confirmation.\& A later rebuild is then unprofiled until you collect again.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-yes\fR
.RS 4
With \-\-delete: delete without the y/N prompt (needed without a TTY).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-state\-dir\fR \fIDIR\fR
.RS 4
Override state directory (where `bench toolchain` recorded the GAIN figure).\&
.PP
.RE
\fBShared options:\fR \fB\-\-no\-pager\fR (see SHARED OPTIONS)
.PP
.SS state boot\-entries
.PP
\fBsysforge state boot\-entries\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.PP
Show which systemd\-boot loader entry boots each installed kernel, who owns it (you / sysforge / none) and the entry sysforge cloned it from.\& Read\-only.\&
.PP
\fBShared options:\fR \fB\-\-no\-pager\fR (see SHARED OPTIONS)
.PP
\fBConfiguration:\fR kernel.\&toml (bootloader, boot_entries)
.PP
\fBEnvironment:\fR $SYSFORGE_CONFIG_DIR, $PAGER
.PP
.SS state failed
.PP
\fBsysforge state failed\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.PP
List packages whose last build failed (recorded in build_state.\&toml), with any diagnosed fix.\& Entries auto\-clear on the next successful build, or once the package is removed.\&
.PP
\fB\-\-names\fR
.RS 4
Print only the failed pkgbases, one per line, with no header and no pager (empty when none), for retrying them: sysforge build $(sysforge state failed \-\-names).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-clear\fR \fIPKGBASE\fR
.RS 4
Clear the recorded failure for PKGBASE and exit.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-clear\-all\fR
.RS 4
Clear all recorded failures and exit.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBShared options:\fR \fB\-\-state\-dir\fR, \fB\-\-no\-pager\fR (see SHARED OPTIONS)
.PP
.SS state forget
.PP
\fBsysforge state forget\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIPKG.\&.\&.\&\fR
.PP
Stop maintaining PKG(s): delete their build_state record so `sysforge update` no longer rebuilds them from source, and remember the decision so update does not re\-adopt them (`build` or `packages add` takes one back).\& The installed package is left in place (still pinned by the sf\-build group).\&
.PP
\fBPKG\fR
.RS 4
Package name(s) or pkgbase(s) to stop tracking.\& A pkgbase forgets every split\-package member sharing it.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBShared options:\fR \fB\-\-state\-dir\fR (see SHARED OPTIONS)
.PP
.SS bench
.PP
\fBsysforge bench\fR \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
.PP
Measure whether an optimized build is faster than stock (report only).\&
.PP
.SS bench toolchain
.PP
\fBsysforge bench toolchain\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.PP
Compile a fixed workload with the stock repo clang and the installed sysforge clang, interleaved; report the median, spread and ratio.\& Read\-only: the stock build is unpacked to a temp dir.\&
.PP
\fB\-\-runs\fR \fIN\fR
.RS 4
Timed rounds per compiler (default 5).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-offline\fR
.RS 4
Use the stock package only from the pacman cache; never download.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-state\-dir\fR \fIDIR\fR
.RS 4
Override state directory (where bench.\&toml is recorded).\&
.PP
.RE
.SS artifact
.PP
\fBsysforge artifact\fR \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
.PP
Inventory user\-authored scripts, units, and pacman hooks.\&
.PP
.SS artifact list
.PP
\fBsysforge artifact list\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.PP
List managed artifacts.\&
.PP
\fB\-\-unmanaged\fR
.RS 4
Also show discovered candidates not yet adopted.\&
.PP
.RE
.SS artifact review
.PP
\fBsysforge artifact review\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.PP
Interactively offer discovered candidates for adoption.\&
.PP
\fB\-\-all\fR
.RS 4
Adopt every offerable candidate without prompting.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-include\-unknown\fR
.RS 4
With \-\-all, also adopt candidates of unknown ownership.\&
.PP
.RE
.SS artifact adopt
.PP
\fBsysforge artifact adopt\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIPATH\fR
.PP
Bring a live artifact under management.\&
.PP
\fBPATH\fR
.RS 4
Path to the artifact to adopt.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-class\fR \fIscript\fR|\fIsystemd\-unit\fR|\fIpacman\-hook\fR
.RS 4
Artifact class (inferred from the scan root if omitted).\&
.PP
.RE
.SS artifact edit
.PP
\fBsysforge artifact edit\fR \fINAME\fR
.PP
Edit the managed copy of an artifact.\&
.PP
\fBNAME\fR
.RS 4
Registry name of the artifact.\&
.PP
.RE
.SS artifact deploy
.PP
\fBsysforge artifact deploy\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fI[NAME]\fR
.PP
Push managed content to the live system.\&
.PP
\fBNAME\fR
.RS 4
Registry name of the artifact.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-all\fR
.RS 4
Deploy every managed artifact.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-force\fR
.RS 4
Managed copy wins, discarding the live edit.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-adopt\-live\fR
.RS 4
Live file wins, updating the managed copy.\&
.PP
.RE
.SS artifact remove
.PP
\fBsysforge artifact remove\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fINAME\fR
.PP
Remove an artifact from the live system.\&
.PP
\fBNAME\fR
.RS 4
Registry name of the artifact.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-purge\fR
.RS 4
Also delete the managed copy and registry entry.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-force\fR
.RS 4
Remove even though the live file changed outside sysforge (discards those live\-only edits).\&
.PP
.RE
.SS setup
.PP
\fBsysforge setup\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.PP
Configure system integration (pacman IgnoreGroup for sf\-build; sysforge'\&s pacman hooks), offer a config preset, and save update preferences (plan confirmation, PKGBUILD review, AUR, build sandbox).\&
.PP
\fB\-\-pacman\-conf\fR \fIFILE\fR
.RS 4
Path to pacman.\&conf (default: /etc/pacman.\&conf).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-preset\fR \fIdefaults\fR|\fIperformance\fR|\fIlow\-friction\fR|\fIsecure\fR
.RS 4
Apply a config preset without asking: defaults, performance (faster binaries), low\-friction (fewest prompts) or secure (hardened builds and sources).\&
.PP
.RE
.SS config
.PP
\fBsysforge config\fR \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
.PP
Check, clean or reset the live sysforge config files, or merge shipped\-default changes into them.\&
.PP
.SS config check
.PP
\fBsysforge config check\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.PP
Report settings in the live config files that sysforge retired (renamed keys, refused values) or does not know (misspelt or no longer used).\& Exits 1 when it finds any.\&
.PP
\fB\-\-json\fR
.RS 4
Print one JSON document (schema 1) on stdout instead of the report; the exit code is unchanged.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBShared options:\fR \fB\-\-config\-dir\fR (see SHARED OPTIONS)
.PP
.SS config clean
.PP
\fBsysforge config clean\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.PP
Rewrite retired settings in the live config files: a renamed key takes its new name (or is dropped when the new one is already set), a retired value its replacement.\& Comments are kept.\& Shows the diff and asks first.\&
.PP
\fB\-\-unknown\fR
.RS 4
Also remove settings sysforge does not know (see `config check`).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
.RS 4
Show the diff without writing anything.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBShared options:\fR \fB\-\-config\-dir\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR (see SHARED OPTIONS)
.PP
.SS config reset
.PP
\fBsysforge config reset\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIFILE\fR \fI[KEY.\&.\&.\&]\fR
.PP
Put settings back to the shipped default: each KEY given as SECTION.\&KEY (or KEY for a top\-level one), or with no KEY the whole FILE, keeping the current one as FILE.\&bak\-<time>.\& Shows the diff and asks first.\&
.PP
\fBFILE\fR
.RS 4
Config file to reset (sysforge.\&toml, profiles.\&toml, packages.\&toml, kernel.\&toml or toolchain.\&toml).\&
.PP
.RE
\fBKEY\fR
.RS 4
Keys to reset, such as build.\&jobs; omit to reset the whole file.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
.RS 4
Show the diff without writing anything.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBShared options:\fR \fB\-\-config\-dir\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR (see SHARED OPTIONS)
.PP
.SS config merge
.PP
\fBsysforge config merge\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.PP
Interactively adopt or clear the companions a config upgrade leaves beside sysforge'\&s config files (pacman'\&s .\&pacnew/.\&pacsave, or .\&sfnew).\& pacdiff\-style: view diff, merge in a tool, skip, remove, or overwrite.\& Merge tool: SYSFORGE_MERGE > sysforge.\&toml [ui].\&merge > $DIFFPROG > vimdiff.\&
.PP
\fB\-\-config\-dir\fR \fIDIR\fR
.RS 4
Live config dir to scan (default: $SYSFORGE_CONFIG_DIR, else /etc/sysforge).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
.RS 4
List companion files and their live targets without prompting or merging (non\-interactive; for scripting/CI).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-no\-pager\fR
.RS 4
Don'\&t pipe diffs through $PAGER (default: paginate when stdout is a TTY).\&
.PP
.RE
.SS packages
.PP
\fBsysforge packages\fR \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
.PP
Manage packages.\&toml override entries (list, add, add\-group, remove).\&
.PP
\fBConfiguration:\fR packages.\&toml (read/write)
.PP
\fBEnvironment:\fR $SYSFORGE_CONFIG_DIR
.PP
.SS packages list
.PP
\fBsysforge packages list\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.PP
Show override entries in packages.\&toml.\&
.PP
\fB\-\-orphans\fR
.RS 4
Show only entries whose package is not currently installed.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBShared options:\fR \fB\-\-packages\fR (see SHARED OPTIONS)
.PP
.SS packages add
.PP
\fBsysforge packages add\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIPKG\fR
.PP
Add or update an override entry.\& Requires at least one of \-\-enable\-build\-from\-source / \-\-no\-cache / \-\-reason.\&
.PP
\fBPKG\fR
.RS 4
Package name to add or update.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-source\fR \fIrepo\fR|\fIaur\fR|\fIlocal\fR
.RS 4
Pin routing (metadata; doesn'\&t satisfy validation on its own).\& `local` marks a hand\-maintained PKGBUILD with no remote to sync from.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-enable\-build\-from\-source\fR
.RS 4
Build this repo package from source instead of installing the binary via pacman.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-no\-cache\fR
.RS 4
Build this package with ccache and sccache off.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-reason\fR \fITEXT\fR
.RS 4
Free\-form note attached to the entry.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBShared options:\fR \fB\-\-packages\fR (see SHARED OPTIONS)
.PP
.SS packages add\-group
.PP
\fBsysforge packages add\-group\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIDESKTOP\fR
.PP
Write a curated desktop\-environment package group (installs via '\&sysforge run packages'\&).\&
.PP
\fBDESKTOP\fR
.RS 4
Desktop environment to add (gnome | kde | xfce | mate | cinnamon | lxqt | budgie | cosmic).\&
.PP
.RE
\fBShared options:\fR \fB\-\-packages\fR (see SHARED OPTIONS)
.PP
.SS packages remove
.PP
\fBsysforge packages remove\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIPKG\fR
.PP
Remove an override entry.\&
.PP
\fBPKG\fR
.RS 4
Package name to remove.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBShared options:\fR \fB\-\-packages\fR (see SHARED OPTIONS)
.PP
.SS run
.PP
\fBsysforge run\fR \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
.PP
Build the toolchain, kernel or packages, or run the fresh\-install bootstrap (pipeline, hardware, reconfigure).\&
.PP
.SS run pipeline
.PP
\fBsysforge run pipeline\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.PP
Fresh\-install bootstrap: every stage from install through kernel (1–7).\&
.PP
\fB\-\-resume\fR
.RS 4
Resume from the last checkpoint.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-start\-from\fR \fISTAGE\fR
.RS 4
Start from this stage, marking all prior stages as skipped.\& Useful on a live system: \-\-start\-from reconfigure.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-no\-unified\-log\fR
.RS 4
Disable the unified log file.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-truncate\-log\fR
.RS 4
Truncate the unified log before this run.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-no\-update\fR
.RS 4
Skip the source sync (fetch and fast\-forward) in every stage that builds, and build each tree as checked out.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBShared options:\fR \fB\-\-retry\-failed\fR, \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR, \fB\-\-packages\fR, \fB\-\-state\-dir\fR, \fB\-\-no\-pkg\-log\fR, \fB\-\-log\-dir\fR, \fB\-\-persist\-log\fR, \fB\-\-profile\-conf\fR, \fB\-\-cache\-report\fR, \fB\-\-abi\-check\fR (see SHARED OPTIONS)
.PP
\fBConfiguration:\fR profiles.\&toml, packages.\&toml, toolchain.\&toml, kernel.\&toml, sysforge.\&toml (per stage reached)
.PP
\fBEnvironment:\fR $SYSFORGE_CONFIG_DIR, $SYSFORGE_STATE_DIR
.PP
.SS run hardware
.PP
\fBsysforge run hardware\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.PP
Re\-run hardware detection and refresh hardware_profile.\&toml.\&
.PP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
.RS 4
Show what would be written without writing.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBShared options:\fR \fB\-\-state\-dir\fR (see SHARED OPTIONS)
.PP
\fBConfiguration:\fR writes the hardware profile under the state directory
.PP
\fBEnvironment:\fR $SYSFORGE_STATE_DIR
.PP
.SS run reconfigure
.PP
\fBsysforge run reconfigure\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.PP
Pre\-build checkpoint: review configs, disk, network, GPG, build preview.\&
.PP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
.RS 4
Run all steps non\-interactively without writing any changes.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-packages\fR \fIFILE\fR
.RS 4
Path to packages.\&toml (used by disk and preview steps).\&
.PP
.RE
\fBShared options:\fR \fB\-\-state\-dir\fR (see SHARED OPTIONS)
.PP
\fBConfiguration:\fR profiles.\&toml, packages.\&toml, toolchain.\&toml, kernel.\&toml, sysforge.\&toml (reviewed interactively)
.PP
\fBEnvironment:\fR $SYSFORGE_STATE_DIR, $SYSFORGE_EDITOR (then $EDITOR, $VISUAL)
.PP
.SS run toolchain
.PP
\fBsysforge run toolchain\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.PP
Build and install the LLVM/GCC toolchain from toolchain.\&toml.\&
.PP
\fB\-\-no\-update\fR
.RS 4
Skip the source sync (fetch and fast\-forward) of the toolchain PKGBUILDs and build them as checked out.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-makepkg\fR, \fB\-m\fR \fIFLAGS\fR
.RS 4
Additional makepkg flags appended to each build.\& Example: \-m '\&\-f'\& to force rebuild of already\-built packages.\& Unlike build/update, \-m is required here: bare makepkg flags are not forwarded implicitly on run subcommands.\& Install flags (\-i/\-\-install) are ignored; the toolchain controls which passes install to the system.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-rebuild\-profdata\fR
.RS 4
Force a full 4\-pass PGO build even if compatible profdata already exists.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-reuse\-built\fR
.RS 4
Skip rebuilding a Pass\-3 PGO package whose inputs are unchanged (PKGBUILD, source commit, profdata, flags, compiler, dep versions) and whose built artifact is still on disk.\& Lets a rerun after a late\-package failure reuse the already\-optimized llvm/llvm\-libs instead of rebuilding them.\& Opt\-in; overrides toolchain.\&toml reuse_unchanged.\& Any input change or missing artifact rebuilds.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-bolt\-only\fR
.RS 4
Build nothing: BOLT the llvm build tree the last run left, repackage llvm, then audit, install and verify as usual.\& Refuses unless that tree is the last Pass\-4a build of the PKGBUILD'\&s version.\& Runs even with [bolt] enabled = false; the other [bolt] keys apply.\& Implies \-\-no\-update.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-install\-only\fR
.RS 4
Build nothing: install the packages the last run built (e.\&g.\& after an install step failed or its sudo prompt timed out), with the usual audit, snapshot and verify.\& Refuses unless the last llvm build is the PGO build of the PKGBUILD'\&s version and every package is in PKGDEST.\& Implies \-\-no\-update.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-yes\fR
.RS 4
Answer yes to the PGO confirmation prompts (profdata reuse, staging/pgo_store purge, 4\-pass start, suspicious profdata size).\& Required for non\-interactive PGO runs; without it, a non\-TTY invocation aborts the PGO sub\-flow because PGO is fragile and silent mis\-optimisation is the failure mode.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-allow\-dirty\-llvm\fR
.RS 4
Bypass the LLVM safety pre\-flight refusal on dirty or diverged trees.\& PGO profdata version mismatches cannot be bypassed.\& Note: this only suppresses the refusal and does not modify the tree.\& Use \-\-cleansrc\-force to actually overwrite the local trees with upstream.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-allow\-version\-skew\fR
.RS 4
Override the pre\-build Gate\-1 abort when the in\-tree LLVM PKGBUILDs disagree on pkgver across the lockstep suite (llvm/llvm\-libs/clang/lld/compiler\-rt/polly/openmp).\& By default a skew aborts before building because dependency resolution will fail; this builds anyway.\& spirv\-llvm\-translator and lib32\-* are never part of the skew check.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-allow\-low\-build\-space\fR
.RS 4
Override the pre\-build Gate\-1 abort when a filesystem hosting the staging dirs / pgo_store / build output lacks min_build_free_gb free (default 40 GiB).\& Dangerous: the multi\-hour LLVM build may fail partway with no space left.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-rebuild\-soname\-consumers\fR \fIprompt\fR|\fIauto\fR|\fIoff\fR
.RS 4
What to do when the built libLLVM changes its soname and would break installed consumers (mesa, etc.\&): '\&prompt'\& (default) warns and asks before building; '\&auto'\& approves and rebuilds them after install; '\&off'\& builds the toolchain but leaves consumers for you to rebuild.\& Overrides toolchain.\&toml rebuild_soname_consumers.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-cleansrc\fR
.RS 4
Purge each toolchain package'\&s src dir and re\-clone before building.\& Refuses (per package) if the existing clone has uncommitted changes, ahead\-of\-upstream commits, or no upstream.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBShared options:\fR \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR, \fB\-\-persist\-log\fR, \fB\-\-cache\-report\fR, \fB\-\-abi\-check\fR, \fB\-\-state\-dir\fR, \fB\-\-cleansrc\-force\fR (see SHARED OPTIONS)
.PP
\fBConfiguration:\fR toolchain.\&toml, profiles.\&toml, sysforge.\&toml ([git], [aur], [safety])
.PP
\fBEnvironment:\fR $SYSFORGE_CONFIG_DIR, $SYSFORGE_STATE_DIR, $RUSTUP_TOOLCHAIN
.PP
.SS run packages
.PP
\fBsysforge run packages\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.PP
Build and install non\-kernel packages from packages.\&toml.\&
.PP
\fB\-\-no\-update\fR
.RS 4
Skip the source sync (fetch and fast\-forward) of each package and build it as checked out.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBShared options:\fR \fB\-\-packages\fR, \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR, \fB\-\-retry\-failed\fR, \fB\-\-no\-pkg\-log\fR, \fB\-\-persist\-log\fR, \fB\-\-log\-dir\fR, \fB\-\-cache\-report\fR, \fB\-\-abi\-check\fR, \fB\-\-state\-dir\fR, \fB\-\-profile\-conf\fR (see SHARED OPTIONS)
.PP
\fBConfiguration:\fR packages.\&toml, profiles.\&toml
.PP
\fBEnvironment:\fR $SYSFORGE_CONFIG_DIR, $SYSFORGE_STATE_DIR
.PP
.SS run kernel
.PP
\fBsysforge run kernel\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.PP
Build and install the custom kernel configured in kernel.\&toml.\&
.PP
\fB\-\-no\-update\fR
.RS 4
Skip the source sync (fetch and fast\-forward) of the kernel tree and build it as checked out.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-cleansrc\fR
.RS 4
Purge the kernel src dir and re\-clone before building.\& Refuses if the existing clone has uncommitted changes, ahead\-of\-upstream commits, or no upstream.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-no\-interactive\fR
.RS 4
Disable interactive kconfig (default is interactive: the PKGBUILD'\&s `make nconfig`/`menuconfig`/etc.\& runs as written).\& With this flag, interactive targets are patched to `make olddefconfig` for unattended runs.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-toolchain\fR \fIgcc\fR|\fIllvm\fR
.RS 4
Build the kernel with this toolchain (gcc or llvm).\& Independent of `run toolchain`, so you can keep gcc system\-wide but build the kernel with LLVM (or vice versa).\& Resolution order: this flag > kernel.\&toml compiler > the compiler the last `run toolchain` set up.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-bootloader\fR \fIsystemd\-boot\fR|\fIgrub\fR|\fInone\fR
.RS 4
Override kernel.\&toml bootloader for this invocation (systemd\-boot is the default).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-base\-config\fR \fISRC\fR
.RS 4
Override kernel.\&toml base_config for this run: the starting .\&config before the sysforge.\&config fragment overlay.\& One of '\&pkgbuild'\& (the PKGBUILD'\&s own base), '\&running'\& (the running kernel'\&s config), or a path to a .\&config file.\& Resolution order: this flag > kernel.\&toml base_config > '\&pkgbuild'\& default.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-base\-config\-merge\fR \fIreplace\fR|\fIoverlay\fR
.RS 4
Override kernel.\&toml base_config_merge for this run: '\&replace'\& (default) copies the base over the PKGBUILD'\&s .\&config; '\&overlay'\& merges it on top, so symbols the base does not mention (e.\&g.\& new in this kernel) keep the PKGBUILD'\&s values instead of kconfig defaults.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-headers\fR, \fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
.RS 4
Build the kernel \-headers subpackage (default: on, per kernel.\&toml build_headers).\& \-\-no\-headers drops it from the build; DKMS modules (nvidia\-open\-dkms, virtualbox, …) and any out\-of\-tree module then cannot rebuild and will not load on reboot.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-docs\fR, \fB\-\-no\-docs\fR
.RS 4
Build the kernel \-docs subpackage (default: off, per kernel.\&toml build_docs).\& Pass \-\-docs to build the kernel HTML/man documentation.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-keep\-hotplug\-drivers\fR, \fB\-\-no\-keep\-hotplug\-drivers\fR
.RS 4
Re\-enable hotplug driver classes (USB, USB4/Thunderbolt, MMC/SD, hot\-plug PCI/CardBus, hot\-plug HID) as modules AFTER config minimization, so devices plugged in later still work (default: off, per kernel.\&toml keep_hotplug_drivers).\& Only meaningful when a minimizing kconfig_targets sequence (e.\&g.\& localmodconfig) is set.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-autofdo\fR \fIrecord\fR|\fIcapture\fR|\fIuse\fR
.RS 4
Sample\-based kernel optimization (AutoFDO; LLVM toolchain only), in steps spanning reboots.\& '\&record'\& builds+installs the profiling kernel (e.\&g.\& linux\-sysforge\-profiling); '\&capture'\&, run on that booted kernel, prints the perf and converter commands (no build); '\&use'\& builds the optimized kernel (e.\&g.\& linux\-sysforge\-fdo) beside the plain one.\& Add \-\-propeller for the optional round 2.\& kernel.\&toml [fdo] mode makes a plain run a '\&use'\& build.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-propeller\fR
.RS 4
Round 2: layer Propeller (basic\-block layout) on round 1'\&s AutoFDO profile, which it pins.\& Requires \-\-autofdo; run record, capture and use again with \-\-propeller.\& The use build installs as e.\&g.\& linux\-sysforge\-propeller.\& Recommended over BOLT for the kernel.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-allow\-no\-fallback\fR
.RS 4
Override the boot\-safety guarantee that a fallback kernel (stock linux/linux\-lts with a boot image) exists before installing a custom kernel.\& Without a fallback, a broken custom kernel leaves no recovery path short of a live USB.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-allow\-boot\-audit\-failure\fR
.RS 4
Install even when the pre\-install boot\-critical kconfig audit (Gate 2) fails.\& By default a built kernel that drops the root filesystem / storage controller / core boot infra aborts before install; this flag installs it anyway.\& Dangerous: it can leave the system unbootable.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBShared options:\fR \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR, \fB\-\-cleansrc\-force\fR, \fB\-\-no\-pkg\-log\fR, \fB\-\-persist\-log\fR, \fB\-\-log\-dir\fR, \fB\-\-cache\-report\fR, \fB\-\-abi\-check\fR, \fB\-\-state\-dir\fR, \fB\-\-profile\-conf\fR (see SHARED OPTIONS)
.PP
\fBConfiguration:\fR kernel.\&toml, profiles.\&toml
.PP
\fBEnvironment:\fR $SYSFORGE_CONFIG_DIR, $SYSFORGE_STATE_DIR
.PP
.SS revert\-to\-stock
.PP
\fBsysforge revert\-to\-stock\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIPKG.\&.\&.\&\fR
.PP
Undo a source\-built/optimized package back to the repo version; update will not re\-adopt it until you `build` or `packages add` it.\&
.PP
\fBPKG\fR
.RS 4
Package name(s) to revert (stock or \-sysforge name).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-yes\fR
.RS 4
Skip the confirmation prompt.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
.RS 4
Show the planned revert without making changes.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBShared options:\fR \fB\-\-state\-dir\fR (see SHARED OPTIONS)
.PP
.SS uninstall
.PP
\fBsysforge uninstall\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIPKG.\&.\&.\&\fR
.PP
Remove package(s); demote any sysforge\-tracked ones out of build state.\&
.PP
\fBPKG\fR
.RS 4
Package name(s) to remove (stock or \-sysforge name).\&
.PP
.RE
\fBShared options:\fR \fB\-\-state\-dir\fR (see SHARED OPTIONS)
.PP
.SH FILES
.PP
/etc/sysforge/profiles.\&toml
.RS 4
Flag profiles, match rules, conflict groups, and paths
(pkgbuild_src_dir).\& Overridable per run with \fB\-\-profile\-conf\fR.\&
Read by: \fBbuild\fR, \fBfetch\fR, \fBupdate\fR, \fBresolve\fR, \fBdoctor\fR, \fBenv\fR,
and the \fBrun\fR stages.\&
.PP
.RE
/etc/sysforge/packages.\&toml
.RS 4
Package manifest: build\-rule overrides applied to the live install
set, the [build] table (repo_mode, system_upgrade, review,
pkgbuild_src_dir), and the
bootstrap install list.\& Managed by \fBsysforge packages\fR.\&
Read by: \fBbuild\fR, \fBupdate\fR, \fBrun packages\fR, \fBrun pipeline\fR,
\fBrun reconfigure\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
/etc/sysforge/sysforge.\&toml
.RS 4
General settings: UI, git, failure_handling (auto\-repair behaviour
per scenario), safety.\&
Read by: \fBbuild\fR, \fBfetch\fR, \fBupdate\fR (git/clone settings),
\fBrun toolchain\fR, \fBrun pipeline\fR, \fBrun reconfigure\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
/etc/sysforge/toolchain.\&toml, /etc/sysforge/kernel.\&toml
.RS 4
Opt\-in toolchain and kernel stage configuration (enabled = false by
default in both).\& Every key is documented in the shipped file'\&s
comments.\&
Read by: \fBrun toolchain\fR / \fBrun kernel\fR, \fBrun pipeline\fR,
\fBrun reconfigure\fR, \fBstate boot\-entries\fR, \fBbench toolchain\fR,
\fBstate profiles\fR, and \fBdoctor\fR on the matching axes.\&
.PP
.RE
build_state.\&toml (under the state directory)
.RS 4
Per\-package build records (a superset of pacman \-Q) plus the table
of recorded build failures.\& Inspect with \fBsysforge state\fR; the state
directory resolves from \fB\-\-state\-dir\fR, $SYSFORGE_STATE_DIR, or the
default /var/lib/sysforge.\&
Read by: \fBstate\fR (read/write), \fBbuild\fR, \fBupdate\fR, \fBdoctor\fR, and the
install\-bearing \fBrun\fR stages.\&
.PP
.RE
bench.\&toml (under the state directory)
.RS 4
The last \fBsysforge bench\fR result per target: the stock and installed
versions, the workload and its fingerprint, both medians and the
stock/sysforge ratio.\& Safe to delete.\&
Written by: \fBbench toolchain\fR.\& Read by: \fBstate profiles\fR (GAIN column).\&
.PP
.RE
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.PP
SYSFORGE_STATE_DIR
.RS 4
Override the state directory (stage progress, build_state.\&toml,
logs, sentinels).\& Read by every command that touches build state:
\fBbuild\fR, \fBupdate\fR, \fBstate\fR, \fBlog\fR, \fBdoctor\fR, and the \fBrun\fR stages.\&
.PP
.RE
SYSFORGE_CONFIG_DIR
.RS 4
Override the configuration directory searched before
/etc/sysforge.\& Read by every command that loads a config file (see
FILES).\&
.PP
.RE
SYSFORGE_EDITOR
.RS 4
Editor sysforge opens: \fBrun reconfigure\fR'\&s config review,
\fBartifact edit\fR and \fBconfig merge\fR.\& Checked first, then
sysforge.\&toml [ui] editor, $EDITOR and $VISUAL.\&
.PP
.RE
SYSFORGE_MERGE
.RS 4
Merge tool for \fBconfig merge\fR.\& Checked first, then sysforge.\&toml [ui] merge, $DIFFPROG, then vimdiff.\&
.PP
.RE
SYSFORGE_ASCII
.RS 4
Any non\-empty value prints ASCII in place of decorative glyphs
(arrows, bullets, progress fills), for terminals and fonts without
them.\&
.PP
.RE
SYSFORGE_PGO_STORE
.RS 4
Directory for the toolchain'\&s PGO profiles, used when
toolchain.\&toml sets no pgo_store.\&
.PP
.RE
SYSFORGE_PROFILE_STORE
.RS 4
Root directory of every other profile store (pgo/<pkgbase>,
autofdo, propeller, bolt), used when toolchain.\&toml sets no
profile_store.\&
.PP
.RE
PAGER
.RS 4
Pager for \fBsysforge log\fR, \fBstate\fR listings, and PKGBUILD review
diffs in \fBbuild\fR/\fBupdate\fR (falls back to less \-RF, then more).\&
.PP
.RE
SYSFORGE_PTY_RAW_DUMP (diagnostic)
.RS 4
A file path: every byte a build writes to its terminal is appended
there, after a line giving the terminal size sysforge handed it.\&
For reports about garbled build output.\&
.PP
.RE
SYSFORGE_PROGRESS_TRACE (diagnostic)
.RS 4
A file path: the progress bar logs each repaint, resize and
handover there.\& For reports about the progress bar.\&
.PP
.RE
SYSFORGE_PACMAN_NO_PYALPM (diagnostic)
.RS 4
Any non\-empty value makes sysforge query pacman through the pacman
command rather than pyalpm, to tell a pyalpm problem from a
sysforge one.\&
.PP
.RE
.SH JOURNAL
.PP
Commands that change installed packages or build state (\fBbuild\fR, \fBupdate\fR,
\fBrevert\-to\-stock\fR, \fBuninstall\fR, \fBartifact deploy\fR/\fBremove\fR, \fBstate
repair\fR/\fBforget\fR) write one record to the systemd journal when they finish, with SYSLOG_IDENTIFIER=sysforge and these
fields, so runs can be queried rather than grepped:
.PP
SYSFORGE_VERB
.RS 4
The command, with spaces as dashes for subcommands (build, update,
state\-forget, artifact\-deploy).\&
.PP
.RE
SYSFORGE_TARGET
.RS 4
What it acted on, when it has a subject: pkg:<names> for packages
(space\-separated), mode:<name> for a state operation.\& Absent
otherwise.\&
.PP
.RE
SYSFORGE_EXIT
.RS 4
The exit status.\& Records of a failed run are also logged at
PRIORITY=3 (err), the others at 6 (info).\&
.PP
.RE
For example, \fBjournalctl SYSFORGE_VERB=update\fR lists every update, and
\fBjournalctl SYSLOG_IDENTIFIER=sysforge PRIORITY=3\fR the failed runs.\&
.PP
.SH DISTRIBUTIONS
.PP
SysForge assumes \fBpacman\fR(8) and \fBmakepkg\fR(8), and nothing narrower.\& It has no
distro\-conditional behaviour: distro identity is reported, never branched on.\&
.PP
Arch Linux
.RS 4
The primary supported base.\& Everything is validated here, including
bootstrap/install, kernel staging, and the graphics/DKMS probes.\&
.PP
.RE
CachyOS
.RS 4
A validated derivative, re\-checked each minor release for packaging
invariants, dependency resolution, \fBmakepkg.\&conf\fR(5) handling, and
version comparison.\& The bootstrap, kernel\-staging and graphics/DKMS
features are \fBnot\fR validated here.\&
.PP
.RE
Other Arch derivatives
.RS 4
Expected to work but unvalidated.\& SysForge hardcodes no sync\-repo
names and never replaces the system \fBmakepkg.\&conf\fR(5), so a derivative'\&s
own repos and toolchain defaults are honoured.\&
.PP
.RE
Run \fBsysforge doctor system \-\-distro\fR to see which tier the running system falls in.\&
Anything not Arch\-derived is out of scope.\&
.PP
.SH EXIT STATUS
.PP
0 on success.\& 1 on build/install/verification failure.\& 2 when the user
declines a gate (stale\-sentinel recovery refused, PKGBUILD review aborted).\&
.PP
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Build one package with its matched profile:
.PP
.RS 4
sysforge build htop
.PP
.RE
Update every sysforge\-managed package, resolving VCS pkgver() up front:
.PP
.RS 4
sysforge update \-\-devel
.PP
.RE
Read\-only drift report (no network, no rebuild):
.PP
.RS 4
sysforge update \-\-offline \-\-dry\-run
.PP
.RE
Inspect which profile a PKGBUILD would get and why:
.PP
.RS 4
sysforge resolve mesa\-git \-\-show\-flags
.PP
.RE
Full system health sweep:
.PP
.RS 4
sysforge doctor
.PP
.RE
